# Large raw source downloads are fetched on demand (or by CI) — see each
# subfolder's README — and are NOT committed. Small provenance/verification
# snapshots (probe.json, *.md) ARE committed so upstream drift shows in diffs.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.zip
*.gz
*.7z
*.geojson
*.gpkg
*.shp
*.shx
*.dbf
*.prj
*.cpg
*.xlsx
*.parquet

# VASCAN's Darwin Core Archive — 2.9 MB zipped, ~37 MB unpacked, and refetched
# by `npm run probe:vascan`. Only the probe's summary is committed.
vascan/vascan-dwca.zip
vascan/dwca/

# Plant-SyNZ raw reports, cached by `npm run host-counts:nz`. Only the
# derived counts (host-counts.json) are committed.
plant-synz/cache/

# HOSTS, the full 52 MB download from `npm run hosts:fetch`. Only the derived
# genus-counts.json is committed.
hosts/hosts-raw.json

# …but the per-area HOSTS records for the areas we are actively working are an
# archive we keep (CC0, ~0.5 MB). The exception is named area by area on
# purpose: a blanket `!hosts/records/*.csv` quietly committed 2.2 MB of rows the
# first time four survey areas were added, which is 4.5x the size this carve-out
# was written for. An area measured to answer "does a source exist here?" keeps
# its counts in genus-counts.json and nothing else; it earns a row-level archive
# when a region is actually built on it, and `npm run hosts:fetch` writes one in
# a couple of minutes.
!hosts/records/australia.csv
!hosts/records/southern-africa.csv
!hosts/records/rio-de-la-plata.csv
!hosts/records/new-zealand.csv
